      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, yes. Thank you 😊 I actually changed to doing `\u0026poolSizes.at(poolCount)` (I prefer to use the `at()` method for safer bounds checking when it\u0027s an option), where `poolCount` is initialized to 0 and only incremented when we actually end up adding a pool. \n\nThis should make it such that `VkDescriptorPoolSize` objects get filled out from front to back within the `TArray` of `VkDescriptorPoolSizes`, which is important when we pass the first element of this array into Vulkan. Before, I was filling the pool size objects out at `i`, which can lead to the filled-out pool size objects being separated by null/empty pool size objects.",
